---Performs a HTTP request using the specified parameters and returns the HTTP response in a callback.
---@param url a string of the URL to request
---@param cb the callback function to call after the request is finished
---@param method the HTTP method to use. default: `'GET'`
---@param data a string of data to send with the request. default: `''`
---@param headers a table of request headers. default: `{}`
---@param options a table of options. default `{ followLocation = true }`
function PerformHttpRequest(url: string, cb: (status: number, body: string?, headers: { [string]: string }, errorData: string?) -> any, method: string?, data: string?, headers: table?, options: table?): () end

---This function is an synchronous wrapper around [PerformHttpRequest](https://docs.fivem.net/docs/scripting-reference/runtimes/lua/functions/PerformHttpRequest/) which will await the data internally, preventing the need for callbacks.
---@param url a string of the URL to request
---@param method the HTTP method to use. default: `'GET'`
---@param data a string of data to send with the request. default: `''`
---@param headers a table of request headers. default: `{}`
---@param options a table of options. default `{ followLocation = true }`
---@return status, string? body, table<string, string> headers, string errorData?
function PerformHttpRequestAwait(url: string, method: string?, data: string?, headers: table?, options: table?): (number, string?, { [string]: string }, string) end

